    spec:
  grid: 16x16 [observed], bg=7
  legend:
    position: top-left 4x4 square [observed]
    border_color: 3 [observed], fills bottom row and right column of 4x4 region
    interior: 3x3, contains exactly 3 target colors each placed once, rest bg
    target_colors: 3 distinct colors chosen from {1,2,4,5,6,8,9}
  components:
    type: solid rectangles of non-bg cells (fill ratio = 1.0)
    base_color: 0 fills most cells; colored pixels (from {1,2,4,5,6,8,9}) sprinkled in at 10-55% density
    count: 4-6 non-legend components
    dimensions: 2-9 wide x 3-16 tall
    separation: components separated by >=1 bg cell (no 4-adjacent touching)
    may touch grid edges
  deletion_rule:
    components containing ALL 3 legend target colors are erased (filled with bg)
    deleted: 1-3 components; kept: 3 components [observed]
    kept components must each be missing >=1 legend target color
  output: same-size grid with deleted components replaced by bg; legend and kept components unchanged

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction
  steps:
    1. Pick 3 target colors from {1,2,4,5,6,8,9}; remaining 4 are non-target colors
    2. Build 4x4 legend at (0,0) - border color 3 on bottom row and right column, place each target color once in the 3x3 interior, rest bg
    3. Decide component count (4-6) and split into deleted (1-3) and kept (3)
    4. For each component, pick random bbox dimensions (w in 2-9, h in 3-7); place on grid ensuring >=1 bg gap from legend and all other components
    5. Fill each component's bbox with color 0
    6. For deleted components - sprinkle colored pixels ensuring all 3 target colors appear (plus optionally non-targets)
    7. For kept components - sprinkle colored pixels using a subset of colors that is missing >=1 target color
    8. Colored pixel density 10-55% of component area
    ```

